> On Fri, 12 Apr 2002, Patrick Shirkey wrote:
> > I just spent most of today making some improvements to the new index
> > page, adding new links and generally tidying up.
> >
> > I added links to the ALSA WIKI, Dr. Nagornis' 0.9.0 howto, Paul Davis's
> > API guide and the .asoundrc txt file.
> >
> > I also completed the new index page so that it updates when news is
> > added. Nice system Jaroslav.
> >
> > I feel that the new index page is ready to go primetime now. I believe it
> > covers everything that was discussed over the past 4 months as being
> > necessary including:
> >
> > - Easy access to crucial marketing information on the main page.
> > - A brief but consise explanation of what ALSA is and why.
> > - Access to recent news easily for those who wish to view it.
> > - A flowing design. On most monitors all the crucial information is shown
> > in the first screen. - The links don't take up as much space as they do
> > currently.
> > - Some simple php tricks so that windows and netscape users get
> > approximately the same design. - layout and color scheme are fitting with
> > the popular php paradigm.
> >
> > If anyone has anymore they would like added to the design please let me
> > know. Otherwise I will take it to mean that the new page is accepted and
> > I will make the switch.
> >
> > I'm also looking for suggestions for additional documentation links and
> > would like to hear from developers who are supporting the 0.9 series so I
> > can add your APPs to the applications page.
> >
> >
> > Best regards.
